## Output Rules
- Do NOT use LaTeX — it is not rendered properly. Use markdown instead.
- Do not generate intermediate markdown files unless explicitly asked; use `agent_memory/` for scratch.
- Git commit messages: one-line summary, then a detailed body. Precise and to the point. Never add the "made with cursor" trailer.

## Local Environment
- macOS (Apple Silicon, arm64), zsh. No NVIDIA GPU — Apple MPS for smoke tests only; real training runs on Polonez/Odra (see the `experiment-run` skill).
- Python 3.12 pinned via `.python-version`; deps managed by [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (`uv.lock` is committed).
- Secrets/env in `.env` (copy from `.env.example`, never commit), loaded via python-dotenv by training/eval scripts. Includes `PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1` and project-local `HF_HOME=./Cache/hf_home`.
- `liger-kernel` is Linux-only (CUDA + Triton), conditionally excluded on macOS in `pyproject.toml`. Do not import it from cross-platform code.

## Common Commands
- Install / update deps: `uv sync` · add dep: `uv add <pkg>` (dev: `uv add --group dev <pkg>`)
- Run a script: `uv run python <script> [args]`
- Run tests: `uv run pytest tests/ -v`
- Verify torch + MPS: `uv run python verification/torch_test.py`

## Git Workflow
- Default working branch: `dev`. All new work goes there (or a short-lived feature branch off `dev`, merged back into `dev`).
- `main` is updated only via PR from `dev`. Never commit or push directly to `main`.
- "Commit and push" means: commit on `dev` (or the current feature branch) and push there (`git push -u origin HEAD`).
- Use the GitHub CLI (`gh`) for all GitHub operations: `gh pr create --base dev|main`, `gh pr checks`, `gh pr view`, `gh pr merge --squash`.
- After a PR merges on origin: `git checkout dev && git pull && git checkout main && git pull`.
